    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Description\n\nHello,\r\n\r\nI'm managing my dotfiles using a bare repo at `~/.dotfiles`, with its work tree at `~`. Therefore, I'm never really \"inside a Git repository\", unless I specify `--git-dir=~/.dotfiles`.\r\n\r\nI see that `mini.diff` already appears to query Git in order to determine where my repository is.\r\nWould it be possible to optionally supply `gen_source.git` with a parameter that would specify which Git repository I mean to be using?\r\n\r\nSince the answer to the above question is \"yes\", I suppose what I really mean to ask is: would you be open to accepting a Pull Request that makes this happen? :)\r\n\r\nI don't really want to resort to using the GIT_DIR environment variable, as I will browse different directories within the same Vim instance.\r\n\r\nThank you, and Merry Christmas!",
    "closed_at": "2024-12-26T14:10:13Z",
    "closed_by": {
