        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nAt glance, this is not so simple. There are the following issues:\r\n- The `gen_source.git` returns a single source which then for each buffer does its job: attach, update reference text, detach, apply. So in order for this use case to work, there should be `gen_source.git(opts)` with `opts.compute_git_dir = function(buf_id) ... end` which dynamically computes the location of '.git' directory. Not sure that all this complexity is worth for a rather not-so-common use case.\r\n- As far as I understand, the information about the '.git' directory should be propagated to *all* instances of using Git CLI. That is during: attaching, getting reference text, applying hunks. Which is a bit painful to do.\r\n\r\nToo bad that dynamically setting environment variable (like, on `BufEnter` or `DirChanged` events) doesn't seem like a robust solution, because reference text computation should be able to be computed at any time (for example, if Git index has changed).\r\n\r\nI'll think about it a bit more, but I'd personally much rather find some Git-native solution to this problem. Maybe there is a way of setting `GIT_DIR` like information per working directory (instead of a single environment variable)?",
