        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "What I found is that [this answer](https://stackoverflow.com/a/11856892) seems to make it work with the \"separate Git directory for dotfiles\" kind of use case. It won't make use of bare repo, but seems a bit more straightforward to me:\r\n\r\nIn particular, I managed it to work with the following setup:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nmkdir tmp-home && cd tmp-home\r\ngit init --separate-git-dir=dotfiles\r\necho 'dotfiles' > .gitignore\r\n\r\ngit add .\r\ngit commit -m \"Initial commit\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter that, any \"normal\" workflow works as expected: both 'mini.diff' and 'mini.git'. Maybe this can be a solution to the use case?",
